.TH SDL_ReadS32LE 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ReadS32LE \- Use this function to read 32 bits of little-endian data from an
.BR SDL_IOStream
and return in native format.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_iostream.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_ReadS32LE(SDL_IOStream *src, Sint32 *value);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
SDL byteswaps the data only if necessary, so the data returned will be in the native byte order\[char46]
.PP
This function will return false when the data stream is completely read, and
.BR SDL_GetIOStatus ()
will return
.BR SDL_IO_STATUS_EOF \[char46]
If false is returned and the stream is not at EOF,
.BR SDL_GetIOStatus ()
will return a different error value and
.BR SDL_GetError ()
will offer a human-readable message\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I src
the stream from which to read data\[char46]
.TP
.I value
a pointer filled in with the data read\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on successful read or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
Do not use the same
.BR SDL_IOStream
from two threads at once\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

